{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790717153,"nonce":"uMnxoeCkMW4ZQnYmysFiOt+jw/0=","message":"Reworked ash_native_call to generate all 29,523 integer/f32/f64 argument and return signatures through eight arguments. Calls are split into chunks of 256 cases so rustc handles small functions rather than one enormous match. dispatch now packs values into stack words and shares the typed call table with dispatch_by_pattern. The interpreter packs its native float arguments into stack arrays and calls dispatch_by_pattern directly, removing four temporary Vec allocations per call. cargo test -p ash_native_call passed seven tests, including eight-argument signatures with four-plus mixed floats, all eight FP registers, and f32/f64 returns. Rebuilt Ash passes ChimpMonk DrivenArm and full scalar/SIMD PhysicsChecks with the default hybrid command. Integer-only native dispatch already accepts up to twelve arguments, so mixed-float calls beyond eight remain a separate limit tracked in 69405d8d759bd330499dbdf4c0bbd0753a683213af1b3727cdfdfe1067f50d63.","files":null}]}